# Licence

## Our code — The Unlicense (public domain)

Everything in this repository that we wrote — the application (`src/`), the build and source
tooling (`scripts/`), the Cloudflare Worker (`worker/`), styles, tests and documentation — is
released into the public domain under **The Unlicense**. See the dedication and warranty
disclaimer at the end of this file.

## The source text — per-source licences

The Vedic and other source texts we reference are **not** covered by The Unlicense. Each
vendored source under `sources/` carries its own upstream licence, recorded per file in
`metadata.provenance.license` and summarised in [`sources/README.md`](sources/README.md) and
[`THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md`](THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md):

| Files | Licence |
| :-- | :-- |
| `sources/rigveda-*.json` | **ODbL 1.0** — a Derivative Database from DharmicData. Licence text in [`sources/LICENSE-ODbL.txt`](sources/LICENSE-ODbL.txt). |
| `sources/taittiriya-samhita-4.json`, `sources/taittiriya-aranyaka-*.json` | Permission not yet confirmed (taittiriya.com). |
| `sources/rigveda-khila-sri.json` | Permission not yet confirmed (sanskritdocuments.org). |

If you reuse the source text, comply with **that** source's licence, not this one. The code
that fetches and renders it is ours and is public domain.

